# Files that Linux executes or parses must have LF endings in the working tree.
# The deploy path copies them verbatim (`scp deploy/apply_nginx_cache_headers.sh
# go4pro:~/rpi/` then `bash` on the host), so CRLF arriving there is not cosmetic:
# a shell script gets a "bad interpreter" error, and nginx would read a trailing
# \r as part of a value, silently changing `server_name`. core.autocrlf=true on
# the Windows workstation would otherwise convert these on every checkout, so the
# attribute has to win over that setting.
# deploy/nginx-*.conf is gitignored (see .gitignore), so git cannot normalise it -
# deploy/README.md carries the `sed -i 's/\r$//'` step for that one.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.conf  text eol=lf
